      "writtenOn": "2023-11-23T03:22:18Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It is confusing that we add a new call_list entry but might not trigger phone_state_change()\nWhat looks correct to me for this guard logic is\n\n```\nif !self.mps_qualification_enabled \u0026\u0026 call_list.is_empty()\n```\n\nthe rationale I see is\nif there\u0027s a call source from CRAS, the fake call is already handled. \nif there\u0027s a call source from HID, we should let the telephony protocol to finish it.\nDoes that sound reasonable?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 763,
        "startChar": 45,
        "endLine": 768,
        "endChar": 55
      },
      "revId": "9b6fab5852186af9f1f7cebc3770ac69adb54390",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "79fbb081_d633a66c",
        "filename": "system/gd/rust/linux/stack/src/bluetooth_media.rs",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 768,
      "author": {
        "id": 2012120
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-11-23T05:40:44Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "What if user hang up a call, but we still have other audio stream working?\n\nFor example\n1. User receive incoming call\n2. User start using YouTube play music -\u003e will not add fake call because call list is not empty.\n3. User answer call\n4. User hang up a call\n5. Now Youtube have no sound because no call in the call list.\n\nIf we really want to implemented logic like\n```\nif !self.mps_qualification_enabled \u0026\u0026 call_list.is_empty()\n``` \nThen we also need to add a fake call back to call list when hang up call. This will be super complicated because we mix the life cycle of fake call and HID call together.",
      "parentUuid": "3865e8ca_02108c7d",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 763,
        "startChar": 45,
        "endLine": 768,
        "endChar": 55
      },
      "revId": "9b6fab5852186af9f1f7cebc3770ac69adb54390",
